meta {
  name: Events - Update
  type: http
  seq: 190
}

patch {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/communities/nswswk8w8wso0ko8owwk8k0w/spaces/<cuid of an events space>/events/<cuid of an event>
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "title": "Weekly review office hour (new room)",
    "meeting_url": "https://meet.example.com/new-room",
    "location_visibility": "going",
    "capacity": 40,
    "replay_expected": true
  }
}

docs {
  Changes an event (#1513): the owner, the admins and the host. Each field is optional; the times are checked with the stored values of the absent fields. The slug stays. sequence goes up when the start, the end, the meeting address or the place changes. A change tells nobody. capacity (1 to 5 000, null removes the limit) may go under the number of Yes answers: nobody is removed, and no new Yes passes. With a token, the answer holds capacity only with the ability event-answers:read. replay_expected false keeps the "Replay only" answers that exist. location_visibility going gives the address and the place to the members who answer Yes, the host, the owner and the admins (#1515). Ability events:write.
}
